### PostgreSQL migration

```sql
ALTER TABLE travel_destination
    ADD COLUMN country_code varchar(2);

ALTER TABLE travel_destination
    ADD CONSTRAINT travel_destination_country_code_format_ck
    CHECK (
        country_code IS NULL
        OR country_code ~ '^[A-Z]{2}$'
    );

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX travel_destination_active_country_name_uq
    ON travel_destination (country_code, name)
    WHERE deleted = false;
```

Existing rows remain valid with `NULL`. PostgreSQL permits multiple active rows with `NULL` `country_code`; non-null `(country_code, name)` pairs must be unique among non-deleted rows. Deleted rows do not participate in uniqueness and may reuse active pairs. Verify the actual logical-delete column name (`deleted` above) and table name before applying.
